From: Tom <tom@getimpala.ai>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 13:31:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] [Loader] Per-rank byte-range reader for TP>1 on the
 Run:ai path (env-gated, Experiment 4b)

IMPALA_RANGE_LOADER=1: a probe pass records, per checkpoint tensor and TP rank, the narrow(dim,
start, len) each weight_loader applies before consuming the tensor (meta-device LazySlice
placeholders; cached under VLLM_CACHE_ROOT/impala-range); the real pass then reads only the
dim-0 row ranges for sliced tensors (16 preadv threads into two page-locked 4 GB batch buffers,
one DMA per batch, zero-copy GPU views per tensor) and hands the loader a placeholder that
serves the pre-read slice for exactly the recorded narrow and reads the full tensor on demand
otherwise (correctness does not depend on the probe). IMPALA_RANGE_READER=runai keeps the
Run:ai FileChunks variant (measured too slow: ~0.28 ms per range group).

Measured on GLM-5.2-NVFP4 TP=8 on 8xB300 (vLLM 0.20.2, 232k tensors): bytes per rank 433 -> 213 GB,
weights bit-identical on all 8 ranks, throughput unchanged, but READY only -4...-6 s (-5 %):
with the bytes halved and the DMA batched the stage sits on the per-tensor Python/launch floor
of model.load_weights (~27-34 s for 232k tensors). Kept as an opt-in.

